    "title": "TikTok agrees to daily usage limits for teens after settling for $100 million - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nadeem Sarwar ,\n21 hours ago Social media platforms are having a historical moment of reckoning in 2026, and the latest to join the list is TikTok. The short video platform has settled a lawsuit with the state of Alabama, alleging that the platform is addictive by design, exposed teens to violent and self-harm content, and led to a surge in the number of emergency room visits tied to self-harm. The lawsuit claimed that the company misled with its claims that the platform protects teen users from exposure to risky content. Read full article",
